{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1130059-multiple-familiars-for-shaman","id":1130059,"title":"Multiple familiars for Shaman?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-16T17:47:33-07:00","id":1130059,"title":"Multiple familiars for Shaman?","content":"I was reading the old Spirit Ways book and noticed it mentioned shamans having multiple familiars. Was this an accident or something from an older period in the game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T21:07:24-07:00","id":1130128,"title":"","content":"While we'll have to wait to see if M20 takes a definitive stance, most of the editions of the game consider this possible but extremely rare. You need both familiars that are individually open to sharing a mage, and the mage to have access to enough Quintessence to feed them.<br /> <br /> Since most familiars aren't inclined to share, the game defaults to treating them as things mages only have one of. Shaman's are mages that have one of the easier routes towards this because they're likely to have a powerful spiritual ally to aid in finding multiple compatible critters.<br /> <br /> Also, a full familiar bond is generally one per mage in mechanical terms, a mage might have a slew of strange creatures around that in-character might get called familiars even if only one is mechanically. An Etherite might have a bunch of clockwork intelligent servants bought with the Allies Background, and only one truly special one that's bought with the Familiar Background.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T07:29:00-07:00","id":1130242,"title":"","content":"Also the Retainer Background is excellent for duplicating a Familiar without the Quintessence cost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T08:44:21-07:00","id":1130836,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the answers. I asked because I watched Jeepers Creepers and thought a flock of intelligent ravens following someone around would be nifty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T15:23:28-07:00","id":1130987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1130059-multiple-familiars-for-shaman?p=1130836#post1130836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the answers. I asked because I watched Jeepers Creepers and thought a flock of intelligent ravens following someone around would be nifty.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't need an actual Familiar familiar for that. You can just tame a flock of ravens and cast a bunch of Mind spells on them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T18:41:51-07:00","id":1131054,"title":"","content":"I want them to be intelligent, though. Or at least unnatural.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 08-19-2017, 03:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T19:59:10-07:00","id":1131093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1130059-multiple-familiars-for-shaman?p=1131054#post1131054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want them to be intelligent though. Or at least unnatural.</div> </div> </div> </div>But why, though? You don't need more than one intelligent raven (the rest can be made to follow its orders), and unnatural ravens might be Vulgar.<br /> <br /> Assuming we're married to the idea of a flock of empowered, intelligent ravens, though, we can make them with some regular magick. Mind 5 can give intelligence to however many ravens you can cast it on (without risking a botch or thirty). And Life 3 should allow you to endow the birds with most sorts of physical advantages that they don't already possess. From there, it's a matter of training (or bribing) them into doing your duty, and using combinations of Mind and Correspondence to give them orders from a distance.<br /> <br /> Again, I'd probably designate one raven to be the &quot;leader&quot; of the murder, who is in direct communication with the mage and leads the rest. That one you can make a proper Familiar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T21:51:31-07:00","id":1131121,"title":"","content":"Or just see if your ST is cool with a &quot;swarm&quot; Familiar. We had a lot of fun in a game where one mage's Familiar was a swarm of bees (it wasn't the most serious game ever). Sure, it's a bit easier to make work conceptually with something that can classify as a colony or superorganism, but if the flock itself is the Familiar, each body can have the Familiar's intelligence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T10:02:03-07:00","id":1131327,"title":"","content":"I bet you could even built it with the materials in Ascension's Right Hand with creative interpretation.... Like, say, &quot;Intangible&quot; to represent the fact that killing any one part of the flock doesn't diminish it overall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T10:04:37-07:00","id":1131328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1130059-multiple-familiars-for-shaman?p=1131121#post1131121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We had a lot of fun in a game where one mage's Familiar was a swarm of bees (it wasn't the most serious game ever).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm suddenly loving this idea.... A bee-keeper Verbena with a hive of bees as a Familiar. Maybe some mythic inspiration from the Hittite goddess Hannahanna and her magic &quot;homing bees&quot;....<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T13:05:35-07:00","id":1131397,"title":"","content":"Nice. Though it was more Christopher Lee meets Tony Todd in inspiration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T07:31:18-07:00","id":1131698,"title":"","content":"Just goes to show you how many different directions you can go from one simple hook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}